{
  "$comment": "NEW-2 (owner 2026-10-21: nobody speaks cron): THE schedule picker ×4. An agent's schedule trigger STORES a 5-field cron (`m h dom mon dow`, the server fires it, `agentTrigger`), but every client edits it through these rows and reads it as `scheduleSummary`. The model (`Schedule`): `repeat` = `repeatValues` (minutes | hourly | daily | weekly | monthly; EXP-1363: `minutes` = every `every` minutes, `every` one of `everyValues`), `every` (minutes only; a read carries `defaults.every` otherwise), `minute` 0..59 (unused by minutes), `hour` 0..23 (every repeat but hourly), `weekdays` ISO 1 = Monday .. 7 = Sunday (weekly only: at least one, ascending, unique), `dayOfMonth` 1..`dayOfMonthMax` (monthly only; 28 so no month is skipped). `cronFromSchedule` writes the CANONICAL form (`cronCases`, exact strings): minutes `*/N * * * *`, hourly `m * * * *`, daily `m h * * *`, weekly `m h * * <cron weekdays ascending, comma-joined, Sunday = 0>`, monthly `m h <day> * *`. `scheduleFromCron` (`parseCases`) reads any cron the rows can express — whitespace-tolerant, plain numbers, lists, ranges, `7` for Sunday, any order — (a read carries `weekdays` [] unless weekly and `dayOfMonth` 1 unless monthly; the rows seed `defaults` when a repeat is switched to) and null for everything else (steps other than a minutes `*/N` with N in `everyValues` and every other field `*`, names, a month, a day of month AND weekdays, a day past 28, a minute or hour list, not five fields, out of range): null = a CUSTOM schedule (an MCP-written one): the Repeat row reads `copy.repeat.custom`, a monospace Cron row shows the expression — the only place cron is ever visible — and picking any Repeat replaces it. The rows, top to bottom, identical ×4 (`copy.rows`): Repeat (a single picker over `repeatValues` by `copy.repeat`; `custom` is offered ONLY while the schedule is custom) · Days (weekly: a multi picker over `copy.weekdays`, its value `weekdaysLabel` — `weekdaysLabelCases`: all seven = `copy.weekdaysAll`, Monday–Friday = `copy.weekdaysWork`, Saturday+Sunday = `copy.weekdaysWeekend`, one day = its full name, else the short names joined by ', ') · Day (monthly: `copy.dayOfMonth` for 1..28) · Every (minutes only: a single picker over `everyValues` by `copy.every`) · Minute (hourly: `copy.minuteOfHour` for 0..59) or Time (every other repeat: the 24h `HH:mm` row, its hour and its minute each a picker — never the platform's own time control, which follows the phone's locale) · Time zone (EXP-1363: daily, weekly, monthly and custom ONLY; a minutes or hourly schedule shows no zone row and keeps whatever zone is stored; a searchable single picker over contract `timeZones.names`, seeded with the device's zone; a stored zone off the list is offered as its own row; a search matches the name with `_` and `/` read as spaces) · Cron (custom only, monospace, `copy.cronPlaceholder`). Validation (`copy.errors`): weekly with no day → noDays; a custom cron that is not five fields → cron. `scheduleSummary(cron, tz)` = a Triggers row's text (`summaryCases`): the repeat's `copy.summary` sentence with `{time}` = `HH:mm`, `{minute}` two digits, weekly `{days}` = `weekdaysLabel` (one day reads `weeklyOne` with the full name), a custom cron `copy.summary.custom`; a set zone wraps it in `copy.summary.zoned` (EXP-1363: never a minutes or hourly summary, where a zone means nothing); minutes reads `copy.summary.minutes`. A new schedule = `defaults` (daily at 09:00, Monday–Friday once weekly is picked, day 1 once monthly is). Mirrors: TS `src/schedule-picker.ts`, desktop `domain::schedule_picker`, iOS ExpCore `SchedulePicker.swift`, Android `domain/SchedulePicker.kt`; the rows: web `@exp/ui` `ScheduleFields` (`packages/ui/src/schedule-fields.tsx`), desktop `schedule_fields.rs`, iOS ExpUI `ScheduleFields.swift`, Android `ui/components/ScheduleFields.kt`; styleguide entry `schedule-picker`. EXP-1363 (owner 2026-10-23): every picker's option list SCROLLS inside its popover/sheet (the 60-row Minute list overflowed the dialog on web) and the trigger dialog/sheet body scrolls when its rows outgrow the viewport.",
